    "result_text": "Both findings addressed, tests green. Summary:\n\n**Finding 1 \u2014 duplicated SHA-256\u2192upper-hex helper (agree, fixed).** Extracted a new `util/Sha256Hex.java` with `upperHexPrefix(value, chars)`, matching the existing `util` convention (`LocalityResolver`, `AddressNormalizer`, etc.). Both call sites now use it: `generateCustomerCode` calls `Sha256Hex.upperHexPrefix(telephone + lastName, 8)` and `householdIdFor` calls `upperHexPrefix(key, 16)`. The private `hash8` copy is gone, and the now-unused `MessageDigest`/`NoSuchAlgorithmException`/`StandardCharsets` imports were removed. Both outputs are byte-for-byte identical to before (same `%02X` formatting, same leading-bytes truncation), so no behaviour changed.\n\n**Finding 2 \u2014 stale `countOwnersInCity` Javadoc (agree, fixed).** Updated it to describe its real remaining consumer, the per-city capacity rule (`isCityAtCapacity`), instead of the removed sequence.\n\nThe minor note about the `generateCustomerCode(Owner)` signature needed no action.\n\nVerification: `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. All acceptance behaviour intact.",
